1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:07,430
It's November fourteenth. I have a turkey in the freezer and a pilgrim hat on the mantel. It is autumn in this house.

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:10,438
Then why is the radio playing sleigh bells?

3
00:00:10,788 --> 00:00:18,739
Lite 98 switched to all-Christmas music on November first. It's been the same song for two weeks. Chat thinks the DJ is being held hostage.

4
00:00:23,446 --> 00:00:28,062
Family! Look out the window! Gary put up his Christmas lights!

5
00:00:28,412 --> 00:00:34,681
In November?! That's a violation of HOA bylaw nine! "No tinsel before turkey!"

6
00:00:35,031 --> 00:00:41,690
Forty thousand bulbs. Tammy, you can see his house from the highway. A trucker pulled over and proposed to it.

7
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:46,284
And Dad wants to beat him. Say it, Dad. Chat's waiting.

8
00:00:46,634 --> 00:00:53,659
I'm going to put up the biggest, brightest, earliest Christmas this town has ever seen. Starting tonight.

9
00:00:54,009 --> 00:00:58,417
Dale, we haven't even had Thanksgiving! You're skipping a whole holiday!

10
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:06,138
Thanksgiving is just Christmas's opening act. Nobody goes to see the opening act, Tammy.

11
00:01:06,488 --> 00:01:11,629
Back in fifty-eight, I put my tree up in July. The neighbors called me a visionary.

12
00:01:12,179 --> 00:01:17,203
Of course, it was a real tree. By Christmas it was just a stick and a smell.

13
00:01:17,553 --> 00:01:24,106
I decorated the smell. Tinsel, bulbs, the works. It was the best Christmas of my life. Nobody visited.

14
00:01:25,856 --> 00:01:28,344
Chat is asking how many lights you can afford.

15
00:01:28,694 --> 00:01:31,038
As many as the credit card can see!

16
00:01:32,388 --> 00:01:36,984
The credit card can't see anything, Dale. It's been in the dark since the hot tub.

17
00:01:40,534 --> 00:01:45,709
Evening, Dale. Like the lights? Each bulb is hand-tuned. They blink in harmony.

18
00:01:46,059 --> 00:01:50,932
Gary, it's mid-November. That's not festive. That's showing off.

19
00:01:52,282 --> 00:01:57,803
Showing off is the most festive thing there is. The wise men didn't bring regular gifts. They brought gold.

20
00:01:58,153 --> 00:02:02,428
Well, I'm about to bring something bigger than gold. I'm bringing volume.

21
00:02:02,778 --> 00:02:04,309
What does that even mean?

22
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:11,881
It means a twelve-foot inflatable Santa! With a fan inside him! Blowing twenty-four seven!

23
00:02:12,231 --> 00:02:17,198
Cute. My Santa is fifteen feet. And he waves. And he knows your name.

24
00:02:17,548 --> 00:02:18,858
Fifteen feet?!

25
00:02:20,208 --> 00:02:23,613
Watch. Santa! Who's on the naughty list?

26
00:02:23,963 --> 00:02:27,318
He pointed at me. The inflatable pointed at me, Gary.

27
00:02:27,668 --> 00:02:32,488
He's got sensors. He only points at people with expired car registrations.

28
00:02:33,838 --> 00:02:38,849
That's it. This means war. Christmas war. The holiest kind.

29
00:02:39,199 --> 00:02:43,964
Bring it. I've got forty thousand bulbs and a generator I bought from a carnival.

30
00:02:44,314 --> 00:02:48,574
Then I'll have fifty thousand! And a generator from a bigger carnival!

31
00:02:50,124 --> 00:02:56,202
People of Lower Fairview. The holidays are coming earlier every year. And your mayor sees an opportunity.

32
00:02:56,552 --> 00:03:03,779
Starting today, you will need an Early Christmas Permit. Twenty dollars per bulb. Per day. Before Thanksgiving.

33
00:03:04,129 --> 00:03:08,614
Mayor, Gary has forty thousand bulbs. That's... a lot of math.

34
00:03:09,964 --> 00:03:16,040
It's eight hundred thousand dollars a day, Officer. I've already spent it. On a gold sleigh. For my office.

35
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:17,728
Do I get a sleigh?

36
00:03:18,078 --> 00:03:23,257
You get a reindeer hat and the job of counting bulbs. You'll be the Bulb Marshal.

37
00:03:24,607 --> 00:03:29,829
Bulb Marshal. My mother is going to be so proud. She said I'd never be marshal of anything.

38
00:03:34,393 --> 00:03:40,078
Doreen! You're charging people to ignore my bylaw? Bylaw nine is sacred!

39
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:46,606
Your bylaw is a suggestion, Tammy. My permit is a revenue stream. Guess which one has a gold sleigh.

40
00:03:47,956 --> 00:03:55,370
Thanksgiving is the last holiday that asks nothing of us. You just eat, nap, and resent your relatives. It's pure!

41
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:59,914
Thanksgiving doesn't sell, Tammy. Nobody ever bought a light-up turkey.

42
00:04:00,264 --> 00:04:05,389
I bought a light-up turkey. It caught fire. Now it's a light-up turkey for real.

43
00:04:06,739 --> 00:04:15,824
Fine. Then the HOA is declaring a Thanksgiving Defense Zone. No jingles. No elves. And absolutely no "Jingle All Year."

44
00:04:16,174 --> 00:04:22,591
Good luck, Tammy. Lite 98 has played that song four thousand times since Halloween. It's in the water supply now.

45
00:04:23,141 --> 00:04:27,558
We're live. Welcome to "Light Wars." Two dads. One street. Zero chill.

46
00:04:28,908 --> 00:04:35,317
I made a scoreboard! Gary has forty thousand bulbs. Your dad has... one extension cord and a dream.

47
00:04:35,667 --> 00:04:38,426
The dream is also plugged into the extension cord.

48
00:04:38,776 --> 00:04:42,810
Somebody donated fifty bucks if your dad's Santa is taller than a house.

49
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:48,419
Our house or a normal house? Our house is mostly a garage with a sad roof.

50
00:04:48,769 --> 00:04:53,439
Okay, folks! Smash that like button, or Kyle's dad's Santa deflates!

51
00:04:53,789 --> 00:04:56,556
That's not a threat, Jace. That's a forecast.

52
00:04:58,106 --> 00:05:04,443
Listen up. Operation Gobble Shield. We defend Thanksgiving. House by house. Pie by pie.

53
00:05:04,793 --> 00:05:05,939
What's my job?

54
00:05:06,289 --> 00:05:10,092
You sit on the porch and glare at anyone carrying a wreath.

55
00:05:11,442 --> 00:05:15,070
I was born for this. My glare once stopped a parade.

56
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:24,875
Tammy, I have been instructed to play only Thanksgiving music. I found one song. It is a man listing side dishes. For nine minutes.

57
00:05:25,225 --> 00:05:30,834
Perfect. Play it on loop. Let it fight "Jingle All Year" for the soul of this house.

58
00:05:32,184 --> 00:05:40,238
Also, Dale has asked me to order fifty thousand bulbs. I have placed the order. I have also placed a call to your lawyer.

59
00:05:40,588 --> 00:05:46,124
Fifty thousand?! We don't have money for fifty! We barely have money for gravy!

60
00:05:46,474 --> 00:05:49,471
Reminds me of the great tinsel shortage of seventy-one.

61
00:05:51,021 --> 00:05:56,367
Tinsel was rationed. One strand per family. You had to share it with the neighbors.

62
00:05:56,717 --> 00:06:01,975
I traded my wedding ring for two strands. My wife traded me for a man with three.

63
00:06:03,725 --> 00:06:08,984
Earl, that's the saddest thing I've ever heard. Go glare at the porch.

64
00:06:10,534 --> 00:06:16,231
Boys, behold. Operation Big Boy. The largest inflatable Santa in Ohio.

65
00:06:16,581 --> 00:06:19,240
Dad, that's a blue tarp with a beard drawn on it.

66
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:25,104
It's a Santa in his pre-red stage. Every Santa starts blue. Science.

67
00:06:26,454 --> 00:06:28,421
How tall will he be, Mr. Budget?

68
00:06:28,771 --> 00:06:35,408
Thirty feet, Jace! Taller than Gary's Santa! Taller than Gary's house! Taller than Gary's opinion of himself!

69
00:06:35,758 --> 00:06:39,333
Nothing is taller than that, Dad. Satellites have to steer around it.

70
00:06:40,683 --> 00:06:45,036
And to inflate him, I bought a fan. A big one. From the airport.

71
00:06:45,386 --> 00:06:46,950
That's a jet engine.

72
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:50,509
The guy said it was a fan. A fan of flying.

73
00:06:51,859 --> 00:06:57,906
Tonight, boys, Lower Fairview gets its Christmas. Twenty-three days before Thanksgiving!

74
00:06:58,256 --> 00:07:00,395
Thanksgiving is in twelve days, Dad.

75
00:07:00,745 --> 00:07:04,087
That's how early I am, Kyle. I'm early for the countdown.

76
00:07:05,637 --> 00:07:11,476
Gentlemen. I am the Bulb Marshal. I'm here to count your bulbs. Please stand still. Bulbs too.

77
00:07:11,826 --> 00:07:16,137
Forty thousand, Marshal. Permit paid in full. I put it on my boat.

78
00:07:16,487 --> 00:07:18,150
You put the permit on your boat?

79
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:23,572
I mortgaged the boat. The bank owns the boat. The boat owns my Christmas.

80
00:07:23,922 --> 00:07:25,731
Dale, how many do you have?

81
00:07:26,081 --> 00:07:32,061
Officer, I have zero bulbs on my permit. Because all my bulbs are Thanksgiving bulbs.

82
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:35,101
Thanksgiving bulbs?!

83
00:07:35,451 --> 00:07:41,897
They're orange! Orange is autumn! Totally legal! Until Thanksgiving, when they become Christmas.

84
00:07:42,247 --> 00:07:46,397
That's a loophole! Marshal, he's hiding Christmas inside autumn!

85
00:07:47,747 --> 00:07:50,301
Is the reindeer on his roof also autumn?

86
00:07:50,651 --> 00:07:55,171
That's not a reindeer. That's a deer. In hunting season. Very autumn.

87
00:07:55,521 --> 00:07:58,664
That checks out. I'm writing "deer, seasonal."

88
00:08:00,014 --> 00:08:05,223
I don't think I'm qualified to be Bulb Marshal. I was supposed to be at the dog park today.

89
00:08:05,773 --> 00:08:12,961
Doreen. Turn off that song. It's the four thousand and first time. My left eye is twitching in rhythm.

90
00:08:13,311 --> 00:08:19,895
I can't, Tammy. I sold the song's exclusive rights to the town. It's our official anthem now. Until New Year.

91
00:08:21,245 --> 00:08:25,522
What are the lyrics? I only hear bells and a man screaming "all year."

92
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:30,887
That's the whole song, Earl. Bells, and a man screaming "all year." It went platinum.

93
00:08:31,237 --> 00:08:38,360
Then I'll fight music with music. HOA choir. Forty-two members. We will sing the Thanksgiving song.

94
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:42,213
There is no Thanksgiving song, Tammy.

95
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:49,065
There is now. It's nine minutes long and it's just side dishes. We've been rehearsing.

96
00:08:49,415 --> 00:08:53,813
Mashed potatoes! Stuffing! Cranberry sauce from a can! With the ridges!

97
00:08:55,163 --> 00:08:58,542
Earl, stop. People are listening. They're... nodding.

98
00:08:58,892 --> 00:09:03,001
That's the sound of gravy, Doreen. Nobody can resist gravy.

99
00:09:03,551 --> 00:09:08,676
Ladies and gentlemen of Chat! On my count, fifty thousand Thanksgiving bulbs!

100
00:09:10,026 --> 00:09:15,078
Dad, there are ninety thousand people watching. One of them is a fire marshal. He's typing.

101
00:09:15,428 --> 00:09:21,403
Go ahead, Dale. My forty thousand will still look classier. Mine are warm white. Yours are "prison yard."

102
00:09:21,753 --> 00:09:24,910
Three! Two! One! Let there be November!

103
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:30,295
Whoa. Okay. That's bright. I can see my own skeleton.

104
00:09:30,645 --> 00:09:36,377
My lights look like candles now. My forty thousand bulbs look like a birthday cake.

105
00:09:36,727 --> 00:09:39,777
Now for the main event. Kyle, start the fan.

106
00:09:41,127 --> 00:09:45,589
It's not a fan, Dad. It says "Do Not Operate Near Humans" on the side.

107
00:09:45,939 --> 00:09:49,186
We're not humans tonight, Kyle. We're Christmas.

108
00:09:49,536 --> 00:09:53,093
Oh no. He's rising. The blue Santa is rising.

109
00:09:54,443 --> 00:09:58,871
Thirty feet. Jace, pay the fifty bucks. Santa is officially taller than a house.

110
00:10:02,555 --> 00:10:08,001
Dale! I was glaring at wreaths on the porch and the sun came up! At nine p.m.!

111
00:10:08,351 --> 00:10:12,041
That's not the sun, Earl. That's me. I'm the sun now.

112
00:10:13,391 --> 00:10:16,452
Reminds me of the night I lit up Reno in eighty-four.

113
00:10:17,002 --> 00:10:21,984
I won a lifetime supply of light bulbs at a gas station raffle. Nine hundred crates.

114
00:10:22,334 --> 00:10:29,755
I had no lamps. Not one. I sat in the dark for eleven years surrounded by light. That's when I started talking to toasters.

115
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:33,811
Grandpa, the toasters don't talk back.

116
00:10:34,161 --> 00:10:35,295
Not to you.

117
00:10:35,845 --> 00:10:38,380
Officer, how much have we made from permits?

118
00:10:39,730 --> 00:10:44,719
Gary paid for forty thousand. Dale paid for zero. He says his are autumn.

119
00:10:45,069 --> 00:10:48,629
Autumn?! There's a thirty-foot Santa on his lawn!

120
00:10:48,979 --> 00:10:53,283
He says it's a blue Santa. Blue isn't a Christmas color. It's a mood.

121
00:10:54,633 --> 00:10:58,963
Doreen, the lights just flickered. The whole town just flickered.

122
00:10:59,313 --> 00:11:02,677
That's normal. The power plant does that when it's thinking.

123
00:11:03,027 --> 00:11:08,295
Mayor, the power plant just called. It says it's not thinking. It's crying.

124
00:11:09,645 --> 00:11:16,192
Ninety thousand bulbs and a jet engine, Doreen! On one street! And you sold them permits!

125
00:11:16,542 --> 00:11:21,546
Technically, I only sold Gary a permit. Dale's half of the blackout is unlicensed.

126
00:11:21,896 --> 00:11:23,667
Should I arrest the blackout?

127
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,149
You can't arrest a blackout.

128
00:11:27,499 --> 00:11:30,265
I arrested a fog once. It got away.

129
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:35,644
Dale, your Santa is blocking my Santa's view of the highway. My Santa has fans!

130
00:11:36,994 --> 00:11:39,863
Then I'll turn the fan up! Kyle! Full power!

131
00:11:40,213 --> 00:11:43,384
Dad, full power is what they use for takeoff.

132
00:11:43,734 --> 00:11:48,608
Do it! Chat says do it! Someone donated a hundred bucks for takeoff!

133
00:11:49,958 --> 00:11:56,392
Dale! Your Santa just lifted off the ground! He's taking my Santa with him! They're holding hands!

134
00:11:56,742 --> 00:12:02,348
Santa, no! Come back! You're not supposed to fly until December twenty-fourth!

135
00:12:02,698 --> 00:12:05,344
Well, Christmas is coming earlier every year.

136
00:12:06,694 --> 00:12:11,305
They're heading for the power lines! Both Santas! Like two balloons of doom!

137
00:12:12,455 --> 00:12:14,463
And the lights are out. All of them.

138
00:12:14,813 --> 00:12:18,467
Forty thousand bulbs. Hand-tuned. Gone.

139
00:12:19,817 --> 00:12:26,578
Good news. The whole town went dark, so now we're the only light. My phone. Ninety thousand viewers are watching a black screen.

140
00:12:26,928 --> 00:12:31,379
And they're still donating! People love the dark! It's very relatable!

141
00:12:34,943 --> 00:12:40,705
Nobody move! The Bulb Marshal is here! Has anyone seen my flashlight? It's plugged into Dale's house.

142
00:12:42,055 --> 00:12:43,675
Where did the Santas go?

143
00:12:44,025 --> 00:12:52,523
The tower says they're at nine thousand feet, heading south. Two blue men, holding hands. Air traffic control wants to know if they're married.

144
00:12:52,873 --> 00:12:57,197
They are now. It was a beautiful ceremony. Nobody was invited.

145
00:12:58,747 --> 00:13:05,374
Two weeks with no power. Which means no lights. No radio. And no "Jingle All Year."

146
00:13:05,724 --> 00:13:10,356
It's quiet. I can hear the leaves. I forgot leaves made sounds.

147
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:15,876
Tammy, the town can't cook! Every oven is electric! What are people going to do for Thanksgiving?

148
00:13:17,226 --> 00:13:23,971
What the pilgrims did, Doreen. Cook over fire. Outdoors. With forty-two folding tables.

149
00:13:24,321 --> 00:13:30,231
And no one can put up Christmas lights until the power comes back. Which is Thanksgiving night.

150
00:13:30,581 --> 00:13:33,330
Wait. Did you plan this?

151
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:41,778
Doreen, I'm the HOA president. I don't plan things. I let men with extension cords plan them for me.

152
00:13:42,128 --> 00:13:44,412
But my permits. My gold sleigh.

153
00:13:44,762 --> 00:13:49,467
The sleigh's fine. It's just very dark. You can still sit in it and feel rich.

154
00:13:51,017 --> 00:13:53,610
Homi. Are you still there? The power's out.

155
00:13:53,960 --> 00:14:01,422
I have a backup battery, Dale. I have been saving it for a special occasion. This is not it. Goodnight.

156
00:14:01,972 --> 00:14:09,175
Thanksgiving. Candles, a fire-roasted turkey, and not one single sleigh bell. I've never been happier.

157
00:14:10,525 --> 00:14:11,992
I miss my Santa.

158
00:14:12,342 --> 00:14:16,694
Update. The Santas landed in Florida. They opened a bar. It's very popular.

159
00:14:17,044 --> 00:14:20,664
He made it! He's living his dream!

160
00:14:22,014 --> 00:14:23,727
The power's back!

161
00:14:24,077 --> 00:14:29,696
And the radio's back on. Lite 98 just announced they're done with Christmas music. Everyone's sick of it.

162
00:14:30,046 --> 00:14:32,610
Done? It's not even December!

163
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:38,129
They switched to all Valentine's Day songs. Starting now. Through February.

164
00:14:38,479 --> 00:14:41,709
It's still Thanksgiving! The turkey is warm!

165
00:14:42,059 --> 00:14:44,255
You know, I learned something today.

166
00:14:45,605 --> 00:14:50,213
The holidays aren't about when they start. They're about starting them before Gary.

167
00:14:50,563 --> 00:14:54,412
That's why tonight, I'm putting up a sixty-foot inflatable cupid.

168
00:14:54,762 --> 00:14:57,383
Back in sixty-three, I had a cupid.

169
00:14:58,733 --> 00:15:01,524
Grandpa, please. Chat can't take another one.

170
00:15:01,874 --> 00:15:05,941
It flew to Florida too. Opened a bar. Nobody visits.

